#!/opt/bin/perl

=head1 NAME

mcp-ask-user - ask the human questions through MCP

=head1 SYNOPSIS

   mcp-ask-user --stdio
   mcp-ask-user --name questions --print-url

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<mcp-ask-user> lets an assistant ask you a question when it needs
clarification or a choice before continuing. C<ask-user> asks one question;
C<ask-form> accepts a generic MCP form schema. By default, a local helper
displays the form using YAD or a terminal and returns your answer to the
caller. C<--ask mcp> uses your MCP
client's form interface instead.

Each C<ask-user> call asks one question, with up to three suggested answers
and a free-text answer field. You can also decline or cancel the question;
these are returned as distinct results.

Run it as an MCP server connected to your client, or include it among the
servers configured in C<mcp-multibroker>. A spawned instance delegates
presentation to that broker unless you explicitly give it C<--ask>.
The broker's ask mode then selects local prompting or upstream elicitation.
See L<AnyEvent::MCP::Intro> for configuring server connections.

=head1 FIRST USE

Configure your MCP client to launch C<mcp-ask-user --stdio>. Then ask
the assistant to call C<ask-user> with these arguments:

   {
     "question": "Which part of the project should we inspect first?",
     "options": [
       {"label": "Tests"},
       {"label": "Documentation"}
     ]
   }

The helper displays a question and returns the chosen or typed answer.
By default its dialog appears B<on the server machine>, not necessarily
where you are using the MCP client. It needs YAD or a usable C</dev/tty>.
For a remote or headless server, C<--ask mcp> works only if the MCP
client supports form elicitation; otherwise configure a local helper.

With a multibroker prefix C<questions>, call C<questions.ask-user>.
A spawned child normally delegates presentation to the broker, whose
C<--ask> mode selects local or client-side forms. Independently run
servers use their own mode. Decline and cancel are distinct results,
not permission grants, and do not cause a fallback prompt.

=head1 ASK-USER TOOL

In C<mcp> mode, the connected client must support the modern input-challenge
protocol and advertise form elicitation. Local prompting also works for
legacy callers and clients without form support.

=over

=item question => $text

Required nonempty question, up to 4096 characters.

=item id => $id

Question identifier, defaulting to C<question>. Starts with an ASCII
letter or underscore, followed by letters, digits, underscores or hyphens,
with a total length of at most 64 characters.

=item header => $text

Optional form heading, up to 64 characters.

=item options => [{ label => $label, description => $description }...]

Up to three suggested answers. Labels must be nonempty, distinct and no
longer than 100 characters. Descriptions are optional, up to 512 characters.
Free text remains available whether or not options are supplied.

=back

An accepted response returns C<{ id, status, answer, source }>, with
C<status> equal to C<answered> and C<source> equal to C<choice> or
C<free_text>. Nonblank free text takes precedence over a selected option;
it is limited to 4096 characters. Decline and cancel return C<{ id, status }>
with C<status> equal to C<declined> or C<cancelled>, without an answer.
An accepted form containing neither an answer nor a selected option is
a tool error.

Input continuations expire after 30 minutes, are bound to the original call
and are consumed once. These results use C<structuredContent> and matching
JSON text; see L<AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Request/result>.

=head1 ASK-FORM TOOL

C<ask-form> exposes the form interface directly when you need several fields
or types other than a single text answer. For example:

   {
      "message": "Choose the download settings.",
      "requestedSchema": {
         "type": "object",
         "required": ["directory", "overwrite"],
         "properties": {
            "directory": {"type": "string", "title": "Destination directory"},
            "overwrite": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Overwrite existing files"}
         }
      }
   }

=over

=item message => $text

Required text explaining what the form asks and why.

=item requestedSchema => { type => "object", properties => { ... }, ... }

Required MCP form schema. Field names identify the returned values.
The tool forwards the schema unchanged, with C<mode> set to C<form>.
The selected renderer determines supported schema features and validates
the entered values. The default local helper supports its documented flat
form subset; unsupported features fail explicitly. Native mode forwards
the schema to the MCP client without imposing the local helper's limits.

=back

The result is the ordinary elicitation response, in C<structuredContent>
and matching JSON text:

   {"action":"accept","content":{"directory":"/tmp/maps","overwrite":false}}
   {"action":"decline"}
   {"action":"cancel"}

The tool checks the response action and requires object content on acceptance;
it does not interpret field names or revalidate content against the schema.
Boolean and numeric values retain their JSON types. Decline and cancel
carry no content and never trigger a fallback prompt. Native continuations
have the same 30-minute lifetime and one-use, original-call binding as
C<ask-user>.

=head1 OPTIONS

Common server options: L<AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Simple/mcp_getoptions>.
HTTP is the default; C<--print-url> prints the authenticated URL without
starting a listener.

=over

=item --ask MODE

Choose human prompting mode: C<helper> (default standalone), C<tty>,
C<yad>, C<mcp> or C<auto>. C<helper> launches
C<anyevent-mcp-form-elicitation> or
C<PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_ELICITATION_HELPER>; C<tty>/C<yad> force that local
interface without fallback. C<mcp> asks client; C<auto> uses client
forms when advertised, otherwise local helper. Declines never retry
via another interface. Explicit C<--ask> overrides inherited
C<PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_PERMISSION_ASK>; spawned multibroker instances
default to client mode. Clients that advertise but silently decline
native forms require C<--ask helper>.

=back

=cut

use common::sense;
use AnyEvent::MCP::Server::Simple;
use AnyEvent ();
use AnyEvent::MCP ();
use JSON::XS ();
use AnyEvent::MCP::Helper ();

my $options = mcp_getoptions ({
   usage       => "Usage: $0 [OPTION]...\n",
   description => "Ask a human question or display an MCP form, locally or through native elicitation.",
   options     => [["--ask MODE", "Ask via helper (default), tty, yad, mcp, or auto"]],
   examples    => "  $0 --stdio\n  $0 --ask mcp --name questions --print-url",
}, "ask=s" => \my $ask_mode);
$ask_mode //= $ENV{PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_MULTIBROKER_PROTOCOL} eq "stdio"
   ? "mcp" : $ENV{PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_PERMISSION_ASK} || "helper";
$ask_mode =~ /\A(?:helper|tty|yad|auto|mcp)\z/ or die "--ask must be helper, tty, yad, auto, or mcp\n";

my %pending;

sub _call {
   my ($req) = @_;

   my %params = %{$req->{params}};
   delete @params{qw(inputResponses requestState _meta)};
   # _meta is per-request context, not stable operation identity: retries can
   # carry different client capabilities, progress tokens and clientInfo.
   # bind the one-use token to the protocol version and semantic parameters.
   JSON::XS->new->canonical->encode ([$req->{protocol_version}, $req->{method}, \%params])
}

sub answer_question {
   my ($req, $id, $labels, $response) = @_;

   ref $response eq "HASH"
      or return $req->error ("Invalid question response");

   my $action = $response->{action};
   return $req->result ({ id => $id, status => "declined" }) if $action eq "decline";
   return $req->result ({ id => $id, status => "cancelled" }) if $action eq "cancel";
   $action eq "accept" && ref $response->{content} eq "HASH"
      or return $req->error ("Invalid question response action");

   my $content = $response->{content};
   my $text = $content->{free_text};
   my $choice = $content->{choice};
   return $req->error ("Invalid free-text answer")
      if defined $text && (ref $text || length $text > 4096);
   return $req->error ("Invalid selected answer")
      if defined $choice && (ref $choice || !$labels->{$choice});

   my $source = $text =~ /\S/ ? "free_text"
              : defined $choice ? "choice"
              : return $req->error ("No answer supplied");

   return $req->result ({
      id     => $id,
      status => "answered",
      answer => $content->{$source},
      source => $source,
   });
}

sub elicit_form {
   my ($req, $form, $key, $done) = @_;

   my $state = $req->{params}{requestState};
   if (defined $state || exists $req->{params}{inputResponses}) {
      my $entry = delete $pending{$state}
         if defined $state && !ref $state;
      $entry && $entry->{call} eq _call ($req)
         or return $req->error ("Invalid or expired $key continuation");

      return $done->($req, $req->{params}{inputResponses}{$key});
   }

   my $caps = $req->{params}{_meta}{"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities"};
   my $native = $req->{protocol_version} ge "2026"
      && ref $caps eq "HASH" && ref $caps->{elicitation} eq "HASH"
      && (!keys %{$caps->{elicitation}} || ref $caps->{elicitation}{form} eq "HASH");

   if ($ask_mode =~ /\A(?:helper|tty|yad)\z/ || $ask_mode eq "auto" && !$native) {
      my $job = AnyEvent::MCP::Helper->new (
         helper => $ask_mode eq "tty" || $ask_mode eq "yad"
            ? ["anyevent-mcp-form-elicitation", "--$ask_mode"]
            : $ENV{PERL_ANYEVENT_MCP_ELICITATION_HELPER} || "anyevent-mcp-form-elicitation",
         timeout => 1800,
      );
      my $old_cancel = $req->{on_cancel};
      $req->{on_cancel} = sub { $job->cancel; $old_cancel->(@_) if $old_cancel };
      $job->ask ($form, sub {
         my ($success, $response) = @_;

         return if $req->{finished};
         return $req->error ($response) unless $success;
         $done->($req, $response);
      });
      return;
   }
   $native or return $req->error ("MCP form elicitation is unavailable for this client");

   my $token = "ae-mcp-$key:" . unpack "H*", AnyEvent::MCP::random_bytes 32;
   my $entry = $pending{$token} = { call => _call ($req) };
   $entry->{timer} = AnyEvent->timer (after => 1800, cb => sub {
      delete $pending{$token};
   });

   $req->reply ({
      resultType    => "input_required",
      requestState  => $token,
      inputRequests => {
         $key => {
            method => "elicitation/create",
            params => $form,
         },
      },
   });
}

sub ask_user {
   my ($req, $args) = @_;

   my $id = $args->{id} // "question";
   my $question = $args->{question};
   my $options = $args->{options} // [];

   !ref $id && $id =~ /\A[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9-]{0,63}\z/
      or return $req->error ("Invalid question id");
   defined $question && !ref $question && $question =~ /\S/ && length $question <= 4096
      or return $req->error ("Question must be a nonempty string");
   return $req->error ("Invalid question header")
      if defined $args->{header} && (ref $args->{header} || length $args->{header} > 64);
   ref $options eq "ARRAY" && @$options <= 3
      or return $req->error ("Invalid answer options");

   my %labels;
   for my $option (@$options) {
      ref $option eq "HASH" && defined $option->{label}
         && !ref $option->{label} && $option->{label} =~ /\S/
         && length $option->{label} <= 100
         && (!defined $option->{description}
            || !ref $option->{description} && length $option->{description} <= 512)
         && !$labels{$option->{label}}++
         or return $req->error ("Invalid answer option");
   }

   my $schema = {
      type       => "object",
      properties => {
         (@$options ? (choice => {
            type  => "string",
            title => "Select an answer (or use free text)",
            enum  => [map $_->{label}, @$options],
         }) : ()),
         free_text => {
            type      => "string",
            title     => @$options ? "Alternative answer (optional)" : "Your answer",
            maxLength => 4096,
         },
      },
      (@$options ? () : (required => ["free_text"])),
   };
   my $message = join "\n",
      (length $args->{header} ? $args->{header} : ()),
      $question,
      map { $_->{label} . (length $_->{description} ? " - $_->{description}" : "") } @$options;

   my $form = { mode => "form", message => $message, requestedSchema => $schema };
   AE::log debug => "ask-user ask-user $id"
      unless defined $req->{params}{requestState};
   elicit_form ($req, $form, question => sub {
      answer_question ($_[0], $id, \%labels, $_[1]);
   });
}

sub answer_form {
   my ($req, $response) = @_;

   ref $response eq "HASH" && defined $response->{action} && !ref $response->{action}
      or return $req->error ("Invalid form response");

   my $action = $response->{action};
   return $req->result ({ action => $action }) if $action eq "decline" || $action eq "cancel";
   $action eq "accept" && ref $response->{content} eq "HASH"
      or return $req->error ("Invalid form response action");

   $req->result ({ action => $action, content => $response->{content} });
}

sub ask_form {
   my ($req, $args) = @_;

   defined $args->{message} && !ref $args->{message}
      or return $req->error ("Form needs a message");

   my $schema = $args->{requestedSchema};
   ref $schema eq "HASH" && $schema->{type} eq "object" && ref $schema->{properties} eq "HASH"
      or return $req->error ("Form needs an object schema with properties");

   AE::log debug => "ask-user ask-form"
      unless defined $req->{params}{requestState};
   elicit_form ($req, {
      mode            => "form",
      message         => $args->{message},
      requestedSchema => $schema,
   }, form => \&answer_form);
}

mcp_tool ask_user =>
   "Ask human question; await answer or distinct decline/cancel status. Configured mode uses local helper or native MCP elicitation.",
   {
      type       => "object",
      required   => ["question"],
      properties => {
         id       => { type => "string", description => "Stable question ID (default: question)" },
         header   => { type => "string", description => "Optional short heading" },
         question => { type => "string", description => "Question shown to human" },
         options => {
            type        => "array",
            maxItems    => 3,
            description => "Up to 3 suggested answers; free text always allowed.",
            items       => {
               type       => "object",
               required   => ["label"],
               properties => {
                  label       => { type => "string" },
                  description => { type => "string" },
               },
            },
         },
      },
   },
   \&ask_user;

mcp_tool ask_form =>
   "Ask human to fill MCP form. Takes message/requestedSchema; returns accept/content, decline or cancel. Configured mode: local helper or native elicitation; local helper supports limited schema subset.",
   {
      type                 => "object",
      required             => ["message", "requestedSchema"],
      additionalProperties => JSON::XS::false,
      properties           => {
         message => {
            type        => "string",
            description => "Form purpose and explanation",
         },
         requestedSchema => {
            type        => "object",
            description => "MCP form schema: object with named properties",
         },
      },
   },
   \&ask_form;

mcp_config
   server_name    => "mcp-ask-user",
   server_version => $AnyEvent::MCP::VERSION,
   short_instructions => "Ask human when input needed: ask-user for question, ask-form for fields. Decline/cancel are not answers.",
   instructions => "Use only when human input needed. ask-user: question, choices, free text. ask-form: MCP form schema. Decline/cancel are not answers.";

mcp_start %$options;
